  "new_commit_message": "Address deployment walkthrough feedback in cloud-network-insights skill.\n\n- Container Monitoring Points: move container install notes under the platform\n  table: `-y`/`-z`/`-n host` defaults (`-n bridge` only when host networking\n  isn't possible), PSC commands with `-e .private.env` right after the\n  subcommand, and legacy docker-compose v1 failures (ask the user before\n  changing host packages; with no Compose, setup.sh uses compose-in-docker).\n- Monitoring policies: scope policies to specific Monitoring Points with a\n  `name` filter (`displayName`), note that `networkMonitoring` is required on\n  Web policies and creates a companion NetworkPath, and add 401\n  troubleshooting (re-mint the token first, then use a service account with a\n  Cloud Network Insights role).\n- Alert policies: always set the `cloud-network-insights: \"true\"` user label so\n  policies appear in the Cloud Network Insights view in the Google Cloud\n  console.\n- Path verification: filter paths by `sourceMonitoringPointId` and describe\n  expected companion and inherited paths.\n- Bump metadata.version to 1.0.1.\n\nPiperOrigin-RevId: 1018890295",
